#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:479
#: 9d690bfbe33f4036a889e2ff532e5ee8
msgid "Serial (serial:)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:481
#: 984574c97349439089a59098968bd7f8
msgid "The serial library provides access to ArduPilot's serial port infrastructure and associated devices and drivers. The script can communicate with a device attached to the autopilot using the ``find_serial(instance)`` function. The script can also itself simulate being a device attached to the autopilot using the ``find_simulated_device(protocol, instance)`` function and ``SCR_SDEV*`` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:483
#: ab3d6f8e05434bb896ee1c59fbcc55b4
msgid "``find_serial(instance)`` - Returns a serial access object that allows a script to interface with a device over a port set to protocol 28 (Scripting) (e.g. ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL``, though CAN/NET/etc ports work as well). Instance 0 is the first such port, instance 1 the second, and so on. If the requested instance is not found, returns ``nil``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:485
#: 6b9e2c60d1344c64b322a1052b5fd23e
msgid "``find_simulated_device(protocol, instance)`` - Returns a serial access object that allows a script to simulate a device attached via a specific protocol. The device protocol is configured by the parameter ``SCR_SDEVx_PROTO``. Instance 0 is the first such protocol, instance 1 the second, and so on. If the requested instance is not found, or the parameter ``SCR_SDEV_EN`` is disabled, returns ``nil``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:487
#: 03d1c0b0d38a42ceb516241cfd6e6070
msgid "The objects returned by the above functions support the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:489
#: 9844aa46d6994841b4ab348b756a0ddc
msgid "``port:begin(baud_rate)`` - Start communication at the given baud rate. Must be called to initialize scripting protocol ports (those from ``find_serial``). No effect for device simulation ports (those from ``find_simulated_device``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:491
#: 7c591f360d7448bd926d51b18b7e24a9
msgid "``port:write(value)`` - Write a single byte. Returns 1 if successful, or 0 if failed (i.e. buffer space full)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:493
#: e5601485467847cca91b49906ccc2a33
msgid "``port:writestring(data)`` - Write a string. The number of bytes actually written, i.e. the length of the written prefix of the string, is returned. It may be 0 up to the length of the string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:495
#: d191af6f731c438e8648a5fb8d75b1aa
msgid "``port:read()`` - Read a single byte. Returns the byte if successful, or -1 if failed (i.e. none available or some other error)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:497
#: 22337eb1ce13409090ad699d8b7f8494
msgid "``port:readstring(count)`` - Read up to ``count`` bytes and return the bytes read as a string. No bytes may be read, in which case a 0-length string is returned. If there is an error, ``nil`` is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:499
#: 42b9e016ae364840923c796240590529
msgid "``port:available()`` - Returns the number of bytes available to read. A read of the given number of bytes may fail on certain errors or if there is another reader (e.g. mavlink passthrough), though these are extremely unlikely occurrences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:501
#: 89a7872c8ee8435f9134c9c86dc2d263
msgid "``port:set_flow_control(fcs)`` - Set flow control setting for scripting protocol ports (those from ``find_serial``). No effect for device simulation ports (those from ``find_simulated_device``). ``fcs`` can be 0 to disable, 1 to enable, or 2 for automatic mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:503
#: 66101dd3209b47b0bc21de62d505b96c
msgid "``port:configure_parity(mode)`` - Configure the UART parity mode for scripting protocol ports (those from ``find_serial``). No effect for device simulation ports (those from ``find_simulated_device``). A value of 0 disables parity (default), 1 enables odd parity, and 2 enables even parity. An internal UART restart may occur when this setting is applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:505
#: d52ec52b63fc4216b6ee60b97ae71498
msgid "``port:set_stop_bits(count)`` - Set the UART stop bit configuration for scripting protocol ports. No effect for device simulation ports. A value of 1 selects one stop bit (default), and a value of 2 selects two stop bits. Invalid values are ignored."
msgstr ""

