#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:558
#: 6da390baae9e43e5a528dbd50ddfd590
msgid "How to Add New Bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:560
#: f21077d919d84c1188663767ab9442a9
msgid "To give Lua scripts access to more features of ArduPilot the API can be extended by creating new bindings. The process is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:562
#: b88597fb8d6e436fa4fce87e12bf3021
msgid "Find the method or function you would like to expose to Lua. For example if you wanted to expose an additional feature of AHRS you would first find the method within `libraries/AP_AHRS/AP_AHRS.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_AHRS/AP_AHRS.h>`__. This can be an already existing method (function) or a method (function) newly added to the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:563
#: f2b9bd6d9173428f8ce9c5c082383dcc
msgid "Edit the `libraries/AP_Scripting/generator/description/bindings.desc <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/generator/description/bindings.desc>`__ and add a new line in the appropriate section for the method, or add a new section if a new class shall be added by following the examples of the other sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:564
#: 9bf53e3fccd64b319fe259fc967bc2cb
msgid "Add the method or function to `libraries/AP_Scripting/docs/docs.lua <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/docs/docs.lua>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:565
#: 67f04a68a29a41f8915046622959581c
msgid "Clean the distribution (./waf distclean) and restart compilation from there as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:568
#: 10198976cccf472e8d0e9681d31ea61d
msgid "Include Lua scripts in firmware directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:570
#: 41c85e77457e4939b3cc35642e6ec313
msgid "Lua scripts may be directly embedded in firmware binaries, rather than being placed on an external SD card. This is useful for manufacturer's to provide the scripts for included peripherals or when the autopilot does not support an SD card. Instructions to do so are on `this link <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/common-oem-customizations.html#>`__."
msgstr ""

